Original change's description:
> [debug] Step into function when OOM break fires at function entry
>
> When the inspector's near-heap-limit callback requests an OOM break and
> the interrupt fires at the function-entry stack check of a function or
> eval, the function's context has not been created and pushed yet.
> Pausing there makes the ScopeIterator observe an inconsistent context
> chain and trips a DCHECK.
>
> Handle kOOM breaks at function entry the same way as scheduled breaks:
> step into the function and pause at the first breakable position after
> the prologue. The original break reasons are preserved across the step
> so the pause is still reported as OOM.
>
> Also extend the ScopeIterator::NeedsContext invariant check to eval
> scopes.
>
